I cannot provide a complete, primary-sourced reference inventory of Vietnam's thermal power plants as requested. My knowledge is parametric and not based on live or document-specific sourcing, and I do not have access to current, verified, plant-level databases with dual-language names, ownership details, technology specifications, and up-to-date status classifications from authoritative primary sources (e.g., EVN, Ministry of Industry and Trade, PDP VIII official documents, or project developer announcements).

Furthermore, compiling such a list requires:
- Access to Vietnam’s Power Development Plan VIII (PDP VIII), which was officially approved in May 2023, and its annexes;
- Cross-referencing with the Electricity Regulatory Authority of Vietnam (ERAV) or EVN’s operational plant lists;
- Verification of LNG terminal-linked gas projects (e.g., from PV Gas, Delta Offshore Energy, etc.);
- Validation of project statuses, which change frequently due to financing, environmental, or policy shifts;
- Accurate Vietnamese-to-English plant name translations, which are not always standardized.

While I can describe general trends (e.g., Vietnam is shifting from coal to LNG and renewables, with many coal projects canceled post-PDP VIII), I cannot reliably populate a full table meeting your specifications with traceable primary sources and URLs without real-time data access or document retrieval capability.

For an authoritative inventory, consult:
1. **PDP VIII (Decision No. 500/QD-TTg, May 15, 2023)** – [https://moit.gov.vn](https://moit.gov.vn)  
2. **EVN Annual Reports** – [https://evn.com.vn](https://evn.com.vn)  
3. **IEA Southeast Asia Energy Outlook** or **Global Energy Observatory** for cross-checked plant data.  

I recommend using the **Global Energy Monitor (GEM) Coal Tracker** and **LNG Tracker** (https://globalenergymonitor.org) as third-party sources that compile primary documentation, though they may not include all Vietnamese-language names or the latest PDP VIII revisions.
